# Problem Encountered

During integration testing, the office workstation was able to successfully ping the Nextcloud server and establish TCP connections on port 443. However, HTTPS requests continuously stalled, preventing access to the Nextcloud web interface.

The following troubleshooting steps were performed:

- Verified Apache service status.
- Confirmed SSL certificate configuration.
- Reviewed pfSense firewall rules.
- Verified routing configuration.
- Tested HTTP and HTTPS using `curl`.
- Confirmed Apache was listening on ports 80 and 443.

Despite these checks, the issue persisted.

---

# Root Cause Analysis

After extensive troubleshooting, the issue was identified as an MTU mismatch on the integration network interface (`enp26s0`).

Although the default MTU value of **1500 bytes** allowed TCP connectivity, HTTPS traffic became unstable due to packet fragmentation, causing SSL communication to stall.

---

# Solution

The MTU value of the integration interface was reduced from:

```
1500
```

to

```
1400
```

After applying the new MTU configuration and restarting the network interface, HTTPS connectivity was immediately restored.

The office workstation successfully accessed the Nextcloud web interface through the pfSense firewall.

